WEBVTT

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:08.120
A FitOut program can tell you when work is
planned, but can it tell you who

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.520
can approve the next decision, what
evidence they need, and what is waiting on

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.680
it? Before committing to work, agree three
things: the business brief, the

00:00:15.680 --> 00:00:18.920
scope of each appointment, and the person
authorised to approve changes.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:23.200
A client-side project manager coordinates
the agreed business workstream.

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.700
Your builder, designers and other
appointed specialists still hold their own

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.240
responsibilities. Take a meeting room
added after pricing.

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:33.280
It may affect more than the partition.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:38.320
Services, lighting, furniture and
technology may all need another look.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.960
Record the connected change, get the
relevant inputs, and approve it before

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.760
updating the baseline. Our free
responsibility worksheet gives you a place

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:47.900
to record those questions.

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.080
Start with the guide, then talk to YOS
about the client-side support your

00:00:52.080 --> 00:00:53.080
project needs.
